    >
      <h1
        class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-h1 css-1kqtlju-MuiTypography-root"
      >
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <div
        class="MuiBox-root css-av31co"
      >
        <p
          class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 css-vdgfig-MuiTypography-root"
        >
          <strong>
            Effective Date:
          </strong>
           January 1, 2022
        </p>
        <p
          class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 css-vdgfig-MuiTypography-root"
        >
          <strong>
            Last Updated:
          </strong>
           November 25, 2026
        </p>
        <p
          class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 css-vdgfig-MuiTypography-root"
        >
          Bldrs Share (“we,” “us,” “our”) provides open-source, browser-first tools for viewing and collaborating on 3D model files (e.g., IFC, STEP) using our Conway Engine. We design our software to minimize data collection and maximize user control.
        </p>
        <h1
          class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-h1 css-1kqtlju-MuiTypography-root"
        >
          1. Information We Collect
        </h1>
        <p
          class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 css-vdgfig-MuiTypography-root"
        >
          Bldrs Share operates 
          <strong>
            without centralized model data storage
          </strong>
          . We do not upload or host user model data by default. What we do receive:
        </p>
        <p
          class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 css-vdgfig-MuiTypography-root"
        >
          <strong>
            Authentication data.
          </strong>
           When you sign in via Auth0/Google or another provider, we receive basic profile information (name, email, avatar) to create or identify your account.
        </p>
        <p
          class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 css-vdgfig-MuiTypography-root"
        >
          <strong>
            Model data.
          </strong>
           Models you open are processed locally in your browser using WebAssembly. If you connect third-party storage (e.g., Google Drive), we only request access to the specific files you select. We do not scan or store other files from your account.
        </p>
        <p
          class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 css-vdgfig-MuiTypography-root"
        >
          <strong>
            Error and reliability reports.
          </strong>
           When something fails, the app reports what failed, the app and browser versions and, if you’re signed in, your account ID, to our error-monitoring service (Sentry). Separately, it counts browsers that can’t run part of the app (for example, with no WebGL) by browser family and device type only, sent to Google Analytics from our server under one shared ID rather than yours. None of these reports set cookies, carry an identifier that follows your browser between visits, or include your models’ file names, paths or contents. They are part of operating the service and are always on, on the basis of our legitimate interest in keeping Bldrs Share secure and working.
        </p>
        <p
          class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 css-vdgfig-MuiTypography-root"
        >
          <strong>
            How models load.
          </strong>
           We don’t use Google Analytics or any other tracking in the app: no analytics cookies, and no identifier that follows your browser between visits. To learn how Bldrs Share is used and how it performs, the app reports each model you open to our server: the kind of file, its size range, where it came from (your computer, GitHub, Google Drive or a web address), how long it took to load, how complex it was, whether it loaded or failed, and whether you’re on a phone or a computer. A report never includes a model’s name, path, web address or contents; the only model it names is one of our own sample models, if that’s what you opened. It carries one random ID that lives only while the page is open, so the models opened in one visit can be counted together; it is never stored, and a reload starts a new one. Our server passes these reports on to Google Analytics under one shared ID, so Google never sees your browser or network address. They are always on, on the basis of our legitimate interest in running and improving the service.
        </p>
        <p
          class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 css-vdgfig-MuiTypography-root"
        >
          <strong>
            Free-use limits.
          </strong>
           Some features have a free allowance. If you’re signed in, we count the private models you open and the models you export against your account, to apply your plan’s limits. If you use the AI assistant without signing in, your browser keeps a random ID our server issued, which expires after 24 hours, and our server keeps a daily hash of your network address, which can’t be linked from one day to the next. Both are used only to apply the free allowance and to stop abuse.
        </p>
        <h1
          class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-h1 css-1kqtlju-MuiTypography-root"
        >
          2. Open-Source and Self-Hosted Use
        </h1>
        <p
          class="MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 css-vdgfig-MuiTypography-root"
        >
